<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I73756c6aa31117a33628625154b4524c29bee1e1" commit="2eb7ba218e9356a8f8b8cd0ddddfb231e3ef96e1" commit_message="event_log: fix uninitialized variable reference  BUG=None TEST=Manually on local machine  Change-Id: I73756c6aa31117a33628625154b4524c29bee1e1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/463688 Commit-Ready: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="463688" owner_email="kitching@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/88/463688/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0fbd3d4995d377f34f28c873c054772ba81fee82" commit="09df2f939a97c32213a3be3a78bd73208351a757" commit_message="daemon_utils: remove invalid pidfile when necessary  When the pidfile contains an invalid string (empty or non-numeric), we should try to recover by removing it.  Traceback (most recent call last):   File &quot;py/instalog/daemon_utils.py&quot;, line 127, in Start     if self.GetPID() and self.IsStopped():   File &quot;py/instalog/daemon_utils.py&quot;, line 105, in GetPID     return int(f.read().strip()) ValueError: invalid literal for int() with base 10: ''  BUG=None TEST=Manually on local machine  Change-Id: I0fbd3d4995d377f34f28c873c054772ba81fee82 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/464027 Commit-Ready: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="464027" owner_email="kitching@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/27/464027/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5e2cc52dbe54854b38bf37b7595cb86b3e27991e" commit="d7c6fb0d82bedbcb104ad7f30a74ce111a9432ab" commit_message="goofy/instalog: run as child process instead of daemonizing  Instalog is started through a Goofy plugin, and as such should be seen as part of Goofy.  Keep Instalog in the same process session, so that factory_restart can handle it without extra code.  BUG=None TEST=pstree -pl TEST=factory_restart  Change-Id: I5e2cc52dbe54854b38bf37b7595cb86b3e27991e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/465788 Commit-Ready: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="465788" owner_email="kitching@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/88/465788/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I949cefd845c8c4e5d0e47a5cfc664652efbdef48" commit="56d385b17d574641c79119a97a4576ec6fab567c" commit_message="factory_restart: use local variables in functions  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I949cefd845c8c4e5d0e47a5cfc664652efbdef48 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/468429 Commit-Ready: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="468429" owner_email="kitching@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/29/468429/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idc78a6c0cfac5a4d48e0107344930d5dcae320fd" commit="c314a55a24e9dade3cf6c42e4fbe44a6a856e996" commit_message="wifi_client: add mac_address_randomization()  Will be used in a few places, but I need to configure it for network_WiFi_HiddenScan and network_WiFi_VisibleScan, which will fail if MAC address randomization is enabled.  BUG=chromium:627552 TEST=none  Change-Id: Idc78a6c0cfac5a4d48e0107344930d5dcae320fd Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/469248 Reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="469248" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/48/469248/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7e6cd6013249e527a5094c342211b55ab375ba55" commit="f89444d7975c87a1256ede7351f054e7d38671fe" commit_message="network_WiFi_{Hidden,Visible}Scan: disable MAC randomization  These tests are looking for the MAC address of the DUT in the packet capture. Don't let randomization screw this up.  BUG=chromium:627552 TEST=network_WiFi_HiddenScan and network_WiFi_VisibleScan on devices      which support MAC randomization (e.g., mwifiex on 4.4)  Change-Id: I7e6cd6013249e527a5094c342211b55ab375ba55 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/469249 Reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="469249" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/49/469249/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I85991f6480c9c5e6c99763f6c51312812b37d5d0" commit="58343f3cb2a50edaeccf17390ec3f2453448b44f" commit_message="UPSTREAM: HID: rmi: Check that the device is a RMI device in suspend and resume callbacks  Commit 092563604217 (&quot;HID: rmi: Disable scanning if the device is not a wake source&quot;) introduced a regression for devices which use hid-rmi to handle composite USB devices. The suspend or resume callbacks are not checking that the device is a RMI device before calling rmi_read or rmi_write. This results in dereferencing uninitialized variables on non RMI devices. This patch checks that the RMI_DEVICE flag is set before sending RMI commands to the device.  Reported-by: Rodrigo Gomes &lt;rodrigo.toste.gomes@gmail.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Andrew Duggan &lt;aduggan@synaptics.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Jiri Kosina &lt;jkosina@suse.cz&gt;  BUG=chromium:706899 TEST=Built and booted caroline, suspended with the device in question  (cherry picked from commit b786ae8e269b5b30fea5efaab8cba32ba9aece61) Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I85991f6480c9c5e6c99763f6c51312812b37d5d0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/467991 Commit-Ready: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="467991" owner_email="dtor@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/91/467991/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I0a6ff4fa67ed8849b777e7abaf77f82d04fb41d4" commit="3726b2a3153c01a02aa8e4d4a2ee3353dbcc8dde" commit_message="CHROMIUM: HID: rmi: only set up inhibit if device is a RMI device  If device is not an RMI device, but a composite device, we should not try to use RMI protocol to access it when inhibiting/uninhibiting.  BUG=chromium:706899 TEST=Built and booted caroline, suspended with the device in question  Change-Id: I0a6ff4fa67ed8849b777e7abaf77f82d04fb41d4 Signed